A||||2||fogglethorpe||taking stock||||1||
Z||000000||fogglethorpe||12-12-2001||04:29 PM||||"Life is what happens while you're busy making other plans" -John Lennon<BR>   This week, I had plans...plans to go to work, deals to make, schemes to carry out. But, this week, life happened when my teenage son was admitted to the hospital with a mysterious illness.<BR>   It has been a week of isolation inside the walls of a sprawling medical campus, a blur of worry and waiting, MRIs, blood tests, strange machines, more worry and waiting, and finally surgery.<BR>   It seems that each individual handles these situations differently. During the surgery, I read voraciously to keep my mind anesthetised against the relentless, gnawing jaws of a beast called fear, until a brilliant, bespectacled man in blue scrubs appeared with good news. I was elated, but perfectly spent.<BR>   This was also a week of education. I learned that nurses are really angels in soft-soled shoes. Ilearned that my son is very brave. I discovered that my wife is an amazing mother. And, I saw that no matter what my trial is, I won't need to look far to see a fellow human being with a much worse one. There's the ten year old boy with black rings under his eyes, sickly and frail and pushing an IV stand down the hall; there's the toddler who looked much too small for his huge hospital bed; and, there's the dazed teenage girl being wheeled out of chemo-therapy on a gurney. These things offer no consolation whatsoever, but they cause me to take stock of the blessings all around me, with the recovery of my oldest son being the most evident one.<BR>   Soon, we will emerge from this great stone fortress of healing into the cool of the day, and make the twenty mile drive homeward. There will be dirty dishes, bills piling up, and siblings bickering over trivial things. Life will become normal again, but will still, somehow, remain forever new...||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-12-2001||10:54 PM||||You really realize how much you can appreciate everything that you have going for you once you are put into a situation like that.  Even though you think things in your life could/should be going a lot better, there are so many other good people who's lives are in a much worse situation.<P>Be thankful for what you have, your health, a loving family, and everything else!||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||12-13-2001||07:31 AM||||I did that with you when you were young,only it didn't last as long.One night of worry about your kids is a lifetime,a week,an eternity.It looks as if you have become me!||||reg||14
